# Walkthrough — Live Screenshot Processing Pipeline Log & Diagnostics

## 1. Summary of Changes

### Live Screenshot Processing Pipeline Log Panel
Added a scrollable, real-time live log panel inside the **Real-Time Monitor Status** card on the dashboard ([`templates/index.html`](file:///c:/github/textline/templates/index.html)):
- Displays every significant stage of screenshot processing with high-precision timestamps (`[HH:MM:SS.mmm]`), stage names (`[API_REQUEST_START]`), and status symbols (`✓`, `→`, `⚠`, `✗`).
- Emits a unique `pipeline_id` for every screenshot processing run (e.g. `20260815-030300-7F31`).
- Displays a final status summary banner upon pipeline termination:
  `FINAL STATUS: ERROR | ERROR CODE: NO_AVAILABLE_MODEL | TOTAL TIME: 88 ms`
- Auto-scrolls to the newest event and caps maximum DOM log entries at 400.
- Includes a **"🗑️ Clear Logs"** button (`clearPipelineLogs()`).

### Backend Event Instrumentation
Instrumented every stage of [`app.py`](file:///c:/github/textline/app.py) with structured `emit_pipeline_log()` calls:
- `SCREENSHOT_DETECTED`
- `CLIPBOARD_READ_START` $\rightarrow$ `CLIPBOARD_READ_SUCCESS`
- `IMAGE_VALIDATION_START` $\rightarrow$ `IMAGE_VALIDATION_SUCCESS`
- `IMAGE_PREPARATION_START` $\rightarrow$ `IMAGE_PREPARATION_SUCCESS`
- `GENERATION_START`
- `KEY_SELECTION_START` $\rightarrow$ `KEY_SELECTED`
- `MODEL_SELECTION_START` $\rightarrow$ `MODEL_SKIPPED`
- `API_REQUEST_START` $\rightarrow$ `API_RESPONSE`
- `MODEL_FALLBACK` / `KEY_FALLBACK`
- `CLIPBOARD_COPY_START` $\rightarrow$ `CLIPBOARD_COPY_SUCCESS`
- `GENERATION_SUCCESS` / `GENERATION_ERROR`
- `PIPELINE_ERROR` $\rightarrow$ `PIPELINE_COMPLETE`

